. In addition it stimulates phosphotyrosine phosphatase and PLC via pertussis toxin insensitive as well as sensitive G proteins. Inhibits calcium entry by suppressing voltage-dependent calcium channels. Acts as the functionally dominant somatostatin receptor in pancreatic alpha- and beta-cells where it mediates the inhibitory effect of somatostatin-14 on hormone secretion. Inhibits cell growth through enhancement of MAPK1 [...] "},{"po":18756,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"2.598003","d":"double"},{"po":18756,"n":"display name","v":"SSTR2"},{"po":18756,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"2.840312","d":"double"},{"po":18756,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"2.495229","d":"double"},{"po":18756,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"1.286360312068112","d":"double"},{"po":18756,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":18756,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"2.863052","d":"double"},{"po":18756,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(117,239,180)"},{"po":18756,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000350198"},{"po":18756,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"2.358579","d":"double"},{"po":18756,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"2.403712","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"padj","v":"1.655856481075353E-6","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":18753,"n":"compartment::golgi apparatus","v":"1.800104","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"1.038753","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"2.416795","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["AF-Q96P50"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":18753,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"1.238882","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":18753,"n":"compartment::peroxisome","v":"0.375","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"tissue::liver","v":"1.232417","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"lfcSE","v":"0.1644028924340647","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"compartment::extracellular","v":"0.421875","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"tissue::stomach","v":"1.193125","d":"double"},{"po":18753,"n":"tissue