tion","v":"Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha; Receptor for interleukin-11. The receptor systems for IL6, LIF, OSM, CNTF, IL11 and CT1 can utilize IL6ST for initiating signal transmission. The IL11/IL11RA/IL6ST complex may be involved in the control of proliferation and/or differentiation of skeletogenic progenitor or other mesenchymal cells. Essential for the normal development of craniofacial bones and teeth. Restricts suture fusion and tooth number."},{"po":18708,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"1.71166","d":"double"},{"po":18708,"n":"display name","v":"IL11RA"},{"po":18708,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"0.906694","d":"double"},{"po":18708,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"1.093422","d":"double"},{"po":18708,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"1.593128337827508","d":"double"},{"po":18708,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":18708,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"2.347434","d":"double"},{"po":18708,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(239,139,117)"},{"po":18708,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000450565"},{"po":18708,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"1.994385","d":"double"},{"po":18708,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"2.427485","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"padj","v":"5.287342191137312E-7","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":18705,"n":"compartment::golgi apparatus","v":"1.739868","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"1.540357","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"4.658392","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["4oli_A","4po6_A","5c03_A","7uyu_A","AF-P29597"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":18705,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"2.502837","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":18705,"n":"compartment::peroxisome","v":"1.762476","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"tissue::liver","v":"3.017414","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"lfcSE","v":"0.1035820274177397","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"compartment::extracellular","v":"4.628375","d":"double"},{"po":18705,"n":"tis